course: dictionary
lesson: 3696
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show you which one is right. This is called context. Read the sentence, then ask: which meaning of the word fits here?
explain: «The barge is a long flat boat on a canal.» Here flat describes the shape of the boat: it is low and level, with no high bumps. The words "boat on a canal" are the clues.
explain: «To hide, the ostrich lies flat with its neck along the ground.» Here flat means stretched out level, not standing up. Check it by swapping in another word, such as "level". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: «Farmers cut flat steps called terraces into the slopes.» Flat means smooth and level here, the opposite of sloping. The steps are flat so they can hold water. The clue is "into the slopes", because a slope is not flat.
fact: Flat means smooth and level, with no bumps or hills.
fact: «A flat tyre» has lost its air, and «a flat drink» has lost its bubbles.
fact: In Britain, «a flat» is a home on one floor of a bigger building; Americans say apartment.
fact: In maths, a flat shape has length and width but no thickness, like a drawing of a square.
fact: «Flat» can also mean exactly, as in «ten seconds flat».
exercise: «The barge is a long flat boat on a canal.» What does flat mean here? | *Smooth and level, with a low shape | Very fast | Full of holes | Sharp and pointy
exercise: Ella says «a flat in London» means a bed. What is a flat? | *A home on one floor of a bigger building | A bed with no pillows | A tyre that has lost its air
exercise: «The runner finished the race in ten seconds flat.» What does flat mean here? | Smooth and level | Slowly | *Exactly | Lost
test: «The bike had a flat tyre, so we walked home.» What does flat mean in this sentence? | *It has lost its air | Full of air | Made of metal | Very shiny
test: «To hide, the ostrich lies flat with its neck along the ground.» What does flat mean here? | *Stretched out level along the ground | Hiding under a hat | Spinning round fast | Standing up tall
exam: Which meaning fits «The rice terraces have flat steps that hold water»? | Without bubbles | *Level and smooth, with no slope | Flat-bottomed, like a boat | On one floor of a building
